      "description": "The DMARC record at _dmarc.kerala.gov.in is not valid: tag fo= appears more than once; tag rua= appears more than once; tag ruf= appears more than once. RFC 7489 forbids this, but does not define what a receiver does with such a record. Implementations vary: some may ignore the record, others may apply the policy they can read. We cannot tell which happens at any given receiver.",
      "impact": "Some receivers may give this domain no DMARC protection at all. Which ones cannot be known from the record.",
      "remediation": "Rewrite the record so it begins 'v=DMARC1; p=<policy>;' - the version tag must come first and the policy tag must immediately follow it. Give each tag once. Other tags may follow in any order.",
      "references": [
        "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7489#section-6.3"
      ],
      "taxonomy": {
        "cwe": [
          "CWE-290"
        ]
      },
